{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"021864d8-618f-468f-bfcc-3be1e34d23f1:0001","subposition":null},"original_role":"assistant","source":"tool_call","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_call\",\"id\":\"fc_01a17a7cf05677c2bc8ea9e00b0806c0\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a17a7cf05677c2bc8ea9e00b0806c0\",\"name\":\"edit_file\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"find\\\":\\\"See [`.env.example`](../.env.example) and the service-level `.env.example` files for exact defaults.\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"wiki/03-Configuration.md\\\",\\\"replace\\\":\\\"See [`.env.example`](../.env.example) and the service-level `.env.example` files for exact defaults.\\\\n\\\\n## Feature flags\\\\n\\\\n- The panel owns flags (`feature_flags` + `feature_flag_rules` tables).\\\\n  Admins manage them at `/feature-flags` in the UI; every change is audit-logged.\\\\n- Consumers (orchestrator `feature_flags.py`, CLI `ipilot flags`, Discord\\\\n  `feature-flags.js`) poll `GET /api/feature-flags/evaluate` every 30 s.\\\\n  Set `FEATURE_FLAGS_ENABLED=true` to opt in; default is `false` (code defaults apply).\\\\n- Kill switch: `POST /api/feature-flags/:key/kill` (or the Kill button, or\\\\n  `ipilot flags kill <key>`) disables a flag in all environments at once.\\\\n- Incident escape hatch: `FEATURE_FLAG_<KEY>=true|false` env var beats the\\\\n  remote value in every consumer; the React app also honours `VITE_FEATURE_FLAG_<KEY>`.\\\"}\"}","truncated":false}
